<!--
  Reference: Copyright (C) 2015, Wazuh Inc.
  Rewrite by m0us3r - https://github.com/mym0us3r/Unified-Sysmon-Configs
  Date: 07/24/2026 Friday

  Sysmon Clipboard Change rules: 100750 - 100760
  Rewritten for Sysmon Native (Windows 11 24H2+)
  Provider: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon
  EID 24: ClipboardChange - ClickFix (T1204.004) detection
  MITRE ATT&CK v15 aligned

  ESCAPING REFERENCE (critical):
    Wazuh decoder doubles backslashes in Windows paths.
    Stored internally: C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe (double backslash)
    PCRE2 to match \\: use \\\\
    Rule: path separators -> \\\\ | regex meta (\s \d \b \.) -> \\

  CONTEXT (2026-07-24):
    ClickFix (T1204.004) is the most common initial-access technique in
    2025-2026 public threat reporting - a fake CAPTCHA/error prompt tricks
    the user into pasting an attacker-controlled clipboard payload into
    Win+R, the Windows Terminal, or the Explorer address bar (FileFix
    variant), then pressing Enter. Used by both nation-state APT groups
    (APT28, Kimsuky, MuddyWater) and ransomware operators (Qilin,
    Interlock). Not this project's own research - public 2026 reporting.

    REQUIRES sysmon-native.xml v1.3+: the prior config excluded
    chrome.exe/msedge.exe/firefox.exe from ClipboardChange telemetry,
    which silenced the exact signal this file depends on (ClickFix's
    clipboard write happens via JavaScript inside the browser). Confirm
    that exclusion has been removed before expecting this file to see
    anything.

  KNOWN LIMITATION - CORRELATION NOT IMPLEMENTED:
    The real ClickFix signature is "clipboard write, then a scripting
    interpreter launched shortly after from explorer.exe or conhost.exe."
    That requires correlating this EID 24 event with a later EID 1 event
    within a short time window. Wazuh's documented mechanism for this
    (if_matched_sid + frequency + timeframe) is built for repeated-match
    /flood detection: the frequency attribute's allowed range is 2-9999
    (confirmed in official docs), and a 2021 Wazuh GitHub issue (#7929)
    confirms if_matched_sid without frequency/timeframe has undocumented,
    unreliable behavior ("fires from the second occurrence onward").
    There is no confirmed, documented way to express "single event A,
    then single event B within N seconds" with this mechanism.
    This file intentionally ships the anchor/visibility rule only. Cross-
    referencing a clipboard change with a following process launch is
    left as a manual Discover/dashboard correlation (both events carry
    the same agent + timestamp) until a verified mechanism is found -
    do not assume rule 100752 or similar exists elsewhere; it does not.

  STRUCTURAL FIX (2026-07-24): anchor 100750 was originally level=6,
  breaking from this project's dominant convention. ClipboardChange
  telemetry is high-volume by nature (any non-Office copy/paste) -
  especially after removing the browser exclusion in sysmon-native.xml
  v1.3, which was necessary for ClickFix visibility but widens normal
  traffic through this anchor considerably. Lowered to level=0; only
  100751 (browser-sourced clipboard writes) alerts.

  MIGRATION NOTES:
    ANCHOR: if_group>sysmon_event_24, assigned by rule 61652 in
    0595-win-sysmon_rules.xml (added 2026-07-24 alongside this file -
    EID 24 previously had no dispatch rule at all).
    This is a NEW file - not yet field-tested. Validate with
    wazuh-analysisd -t and a live test before treating as
    production-confirmed.
-->

<group name="sysmon,sysmon_eid24,windows,">

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       BASE ANCHOR - EID 24 (Clipboard Change)
       Fires on any clipboard write not already excluded at the Sysmon
       config level (Office apps only, per sysmon-native.xml v1.3).
       Level kept moderate (not critical) since this is a visibility
       signal, not a confirmed-malicious one on its own - see the
       KNOWN LIMITATION note above.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100750" level="0">
    <if_group>sysmon_event_24</if_group>
    <field name="win.system.providerName">^Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon$</field>
    <description>Native Sysmon [EID 24]: Clipboard content changed by $(win.eventdata.image)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1204.004</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       T1204.004 - Elevated visibility when the source is a browser
       (the actual ClickFix vector). Still not a confirmation by
       itself - most browser clipboard writes are the user's own
       copy/paste. This raises priority for triage, not severity level.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100751" level="8">
    <if_sid>100750</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\\\(chrome|msedge|firefox)\.exe$</field>
    <description>Clipboard content changed by a browser process - review for ClickFix (T1204.004) if followed by a Run/Terminal paste-execute - $(win.eventdata.image)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1204.004</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

</group>
